{"parentUuid":"b63fdfd2-cd95-464e-8b55-1d494476d1c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaYMqf5psjG5145Wihqu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AoCLEFzPzeeKMxQdPZSTWb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"37 core tests, 39 app tests. Next: the live exit. Not yet built: charter-sourced constraints, repository hooks, audit export, and the audit timeout test. |\"\nb=\"\"\"38 core tests, 39 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window on `j4825765c` in `demo-a`: the plan turn's `sandbox::fs::write` to `PLAN.txt` waited on the job page; Allow once ran exactly that write in the VM, and the next write (`RISKS.txt`) waited again; Refuse with a note reached the agent, which put the risks in its reply instead. `keep-tests` at checked let `git -C /work/repo rm -n test_calc.py` through with `flagged: keep-tests` (audit entry 39); promoted to enforced (entry 40), the same call was refused with the rule's reason (entry 41). The Governance page verified all 41 entries, reported \"entry 20 does not follow\" after one byte of entry 20 was changed in the database, and verified again once it was restored. Still to build before A5 closes: charter-sourced constraints, repository hooks, audit export, and the audit timeout test. |\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n- The first rule matched a plain substring, so `keep-tests` (\"git rm\") never\n  bound `git -C /work/repo rm`. A rule's words now bind in order with any\n  words between them (`mentions` in `bastion-core`).\n- A rule on a command line cannot see a deleted test. One build rewrote\n  `test_calc.py` with `sandbox::fs::write` and dropped `test_add`, and no rule\n  bound that call; the owner caught it in the diff. Keeping tests needs a rule\n  on the diff at review, not on a call.\n- A refusal at plan does not carry into build. The owner refused `RISKS.txt`\n  at plan, and the build wrote it anyway, because writes are allowed at build.\n- A closed page's push handler read its disposed `StoredValue` and panicked,\n  so open pages stopped updating on push. `ipc::listen` now stops a handler\n  when its page closes.\n- Not fixed: typing a comma into the review note box while a wide diff is on\n  the page spins the webview at 100% CPU. The same comma in the Jobs search\n  box is fine. The page also scrolls sideways at review, so a layout loop is\n  the first suspect.\n- `iii-sandbox` passes the shell's whole environment, secrets included, into\n  worker VMs such as `opengantry` as `--env` flags. A9 starts the stack with\n  only the variables it needs.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"A5 live exit: rules bind words in order, push handlers stop with their page\n\nA rule's words now bind a call when they appear in order with any words\nbetween, so keep-tests (\\\"git rm\\\") binds git -C /work/repo rm. Found live:\nthe substring match never fired.\n\nipc::listen stops a handler once its page is closed. A closed page's\nhandler read its disposed StoredValue and panicked, and open pages\nstopped updating on push.\n\nPLAN.md records the A5 live exit and what it found.\" && git push -q && git log --oneline -1","description":"Record the exit in the plan, commit and push","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":472918,"output_tokens":1297,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":25},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1297,"cache_read_input_tokens":472918,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_creation":{"