used `RISKS.txt`\n  at plan, and the build wrote it anyway, because writes are allowed at build.\n- A closed page's push handler read its disposed `StoredValue` and panicked,\n  so open pages stopped updating on push. `ipc::listen` now stops a handler\n  when its page closes.\n- Not fixed: typing a comma into the review note box while a wide diff is on\n  the page spins the webview at 100% CPU. The same comma in the Jobs search\n  box is fine. The page also scrolls sideways at review, so a layout loop is\n  the first suspect.\n- `iii-sandbox` passes the shell's whole environment, secrets included, into\n  worker VMs such as `opengantry` as `--env` flags. A9 starts the stack with\n  only the variables it needs.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"A5 live exit: rules bind words in order, push handlers stop with their page\n\nA rule's words now bind a call when they appear in order with any words\nbetween, so keep-tests (\\\"git rm\\\") binds git -C /work/repo rm. Found live:\nthe substring match never fired.\n\nipc::listen stops a handler once its page is closed. A closed page's\nhandler read its disposed StoredValue and panicked, and open pages\nstopped updating on push.\n\nPLAN.md records the A5 live exit and what it found.\" && git push -q && git log --oneline -1","description":"Record the exit in the plan, commit and push","timeout":120000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01AoCLEFzPzeeKMxQdPZSTWb":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"447b03f4-4e18-4cc4-b213-b73f26d87608","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgaYMqF2kWY5EmpEtF6tj","attributionMcpServer":"plugin:codescene:codescene","attributionMcpTool":"pre_commit_code_health_safeguard","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2e97bf5-2275-4874-8db3-b95f1110559e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:20:55.757Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli",